{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2017-515", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/515", "wordCount": 1288, "segments": [{"start": 17.0, "text": "Welcome, my name is Eryk"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "Vershen, I'm am AVFoundation"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "engineer at Apple."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "This is session 515 which is"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "about HLS authoring and the HLS"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "tools."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "HLS is an abbreviation for HTTP"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Live Streaming."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "HLS is the way you stream"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "content to all Apple devices."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "I'm going to be talking about"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "the document HLS Authoring"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "Specification for Apple Devices"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "and the tools we distribute for"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "creating and validating HLS"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "The Authoring Specification and"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "other important documents about"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "HLS can be found at this URL"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "developer.apple.com/streaming."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "The Authoring Specification is"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "Apple's advice for authoring HLS"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "We wanted the HLS specification,"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "the Internet draft, to include"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "only absolutely necessary"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "requirements."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "The Authoring Specification, on"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "the other hand, includes"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "requirements that are specific"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "to Apple's players, as well as"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "things that, while not"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "absolutely required, are part of"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "best practice."}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "The big news this year is we've"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "added support for HEVC."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "Here are the limits on what is"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "playable."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "Main 10 Profile, Level 5.0, High"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "Tier."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "Now that we support HEVC content"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "we've added bit rate guidelines"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "for that as well."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "You should treat those"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "recommendations as very"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "preliminary."}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "HEVC encoders are still"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "evolving, we expect to see"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "improvements over time so we may"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "revise our guidelines in the"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "future."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "You should also remember that"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "the bit rate recommendations in"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "the Authoring Specification are"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "guidelines, they are not cast in"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "stone."}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "We are aware that all content is"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "different, a bit rate that works"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "for a video of two people"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "talking is not likely to work"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "for a sporting event."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "And you may have different"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "constraints on the number of bit"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "rate variants that you can"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "provide."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "So, use the bit rate guidelines"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "as a starting point."}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "Having HEVC means that you can"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "have both H.264 and HEVC content"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "in the same master playlist."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "So, we've come up with some best"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "practices."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "First and most important, always"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "use the CODECS attribute."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "You need this so that older"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "players don't try to play the"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "HEVC content."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "Second and almost as important,"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "always include some H.264"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "You need this so older players"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "will have something that they"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "can play."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Now the player will switch"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "between H.264 and HEVC."}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "However, for two variants with"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "similar bit rates the player"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "will typically favor the HEVC"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "While H.264 content could be in"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "FMP4 files for maximum"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "compatibility keep your H.264 in"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "transport streams."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "The last point I want to make is"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "that these same rules apply to"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "so-called trick play content,"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "that is I-frame-only content."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "Along with adding HEVC support"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "we also added support for a"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "second subtitle format, IMSC."}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "If you want more detail on our"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "support for IMSC1 you should"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "look at this year's Advances in"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "HTTP Live Streaming talk."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "IMSC1 is based on TTML, the"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "timed text markup language and"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "it's compatible with standards"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "from the EBU and SMPTE."}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "Let's talk about best practices"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "for subtitle content."}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "We support the text profile of"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "IMSC and note that IMSC content"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "must be in fragmented MP4 files,"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "you can't use plaintext files."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "WebVTT is the same as it has"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "been, text files typically"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "having an extension of .VTT or"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": ".webVTT."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "Remember that you can mix up"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "IMSC and webVTT with H.264 HEVC"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "content however you want,"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "they're completely independent."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "You should always use the IMSC1"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "CODECS value."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "Including that value ensures"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "that older clients will ignore"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "the variant. However, for maximum backward"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "compatibilities don't put in the"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "value for the webVTT content."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "I want to change gears and talk"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "about the HLS tools and the"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "changes we've made there."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "The tools are available on the"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "developer site and you can find"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "them through the same URL I"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "mentioned earlier,"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "developer.apple.com/streaming."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "The tools fall into three rough"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "categories, tools for segmenting"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "video and audio, tools for"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "validating content and making"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "validation reports and finally,"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "tools for creating subtitles,"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "iv3 metadata and master"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "playlists."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "Now the validator does not do"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "low-level bitstream checks, you"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "should be using third-party"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "tools if you think you may have"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "issues with your encoders."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "Let's look at some of the"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "specific changes we made in the"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "tools. Well firstly, we've added the"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "ability for MediaStreamValidator"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "to check local files."}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "You no longer have to put an"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "HTTP server to validate your"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "streams."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "If you have direct file access"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "you can check them that way and"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "you can use relative paths,"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "absolute paths or file URLs."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "However, I should note that you"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "can't mix file URLs and HTTP,"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "that is if the master playlist"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "is a file path then the media"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "playlist it references can't be"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "HTTP URLs."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "Of course, we added support for"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "HEVC into the tools."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "We've also made a lot of general"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "improvements to the tools,"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "principally the MediaStreamValidator and HLS"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "report."}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "We check more things about the"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "stream."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "There are too many to list, but"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "for example, we're now validating the CODEC usage."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "We have better handling for"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "errors on the stream during"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "validation."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "And we made the ordering of"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "variants renditions in the"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "reports be more consistent."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "We've added several new options,"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "I want to call out just three of"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "First, the description option on"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "MediaStreamValidator."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "The URLs for a stream don't"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "necessarily make clear what the"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "content is."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "This option allows you to add"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "some text describing the stream."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "For example, such and such show,"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "season two, episode five."}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "The text will appear at the top"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "of the report near the URL."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "For HLS report, we've added some"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "new optional columns."}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "Rather than continue the way we"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "had previously with separate"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "options for each column, instead"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "we've added a columns option"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "that takes a list of column and"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "identifiers."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "The set of available column"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "identifiers can be found using"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "the Help option or in the"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "page."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "The old id and pl options that"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "gave you data id values and"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "playlist bit rates are still"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "supported, but are deprecated in"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "favor of column identifiers."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "And the column identifiers for"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "those are just id and pl."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "Last year we added hdcp-level"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "support, but we forgot to tell"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "you about the hdcp-level option"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "on MediaFileSegmenter."}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "This allows you to set the"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "hdcp-level."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "The hdcp-level is included in"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "the Plist that gets generated by"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "MediaFileSegmenter."}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "And you can pass that Plist to"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "the variant playlist creator to"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "get the hdcp-level attribute in"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "the generated master playlist."}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "Here's a quick look of a sample"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "report."}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "Notice the second line, that's"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "from the description option that"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "we passed in"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "MediaStreamValidator."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "And notice that we've now added"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "a CODECS column so you can see"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "which variants are H.264 and"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "HEVC."}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "Now we use the AVC, the"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "alternate name of H.264 so that"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "we'll have more visible"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "separation between the two CODEC"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "types."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "As part of the changes in the"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "ordering of variants and"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "renditions, we now keep audio,"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "closed caption and subtitle"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "renditions separate."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "To summarize, remember that URL,"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "developer.apple.com/streaming,"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "everything you need to know is"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "pointed to from that page."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Besides the various documents it"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "also has links to sample"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "streams, to the tools download,"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "to past videos about HLS, the"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "information about FairPlay"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Streaming and so on."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "I encourage you all to read the"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "HLS Authoring Specification for"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "Apple Devices and the HLS spec."}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "For more information go to the"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "webpage for this talk,"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "developer.apple.com/WWDC17/515."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "We have some related video"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "sessions, Advances in HTTP Live"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "Streaming."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "This has more discussion of HEVC"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "and IMSC1, as well as some other"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "interesting topics."}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "And Error Handling Best"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "Practices for HTTP Live"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "Streaming. That will help you understand"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "what your server needs to do to"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "be a good HLS server."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "You can watch either of these"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "videos via the web or in the"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "WWDC app."}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "I hope you found the talk"}]}
